>
  <section>
    <h1>Documentation</h1>

    <p>
      This documentation describes how BeaconGuard authorizes governed AI
      transactions: whether an enterprise application may invoke an AI provider
      (Request Admission Authorization), and whether a later declared enterprise
      action based on an AI-generated result may proceed (Result-to-Action
      Authorization). AI output remains an untrusted proposal. Runtime outcomes
      are ALLOW or DENY only under an Active Verified Release.
    </p>

    <p>
      BeaconGuard Verify is a read-only functional domain for investigation,
      reconstruction, replay, and export. Deployment responsibilities are shared
      with the customer. The product remains under controlled internal
      qualification for customer production use.
    </p>

